# Boolean fit gates (scripts/gate.sh): "<part> empty" must render zero
# facets, "<part> interferes" is the mandatory negative control proving the
# check can fail.
#
# This is a print-in-place ball joint: a fused ball scores 100/100 watertight
# and only these interference checks see it. `fitcheck` proves the printed
# pose clears. `fitcheck_tilt` is the articulation proof (the
# perspective-coin fitcheck_flip pattern): the ball+stud swept through the
# whole ±max_tilt cone against the socket — the stud must clear the dome
# aperture at every tilt, which a rest-pose check cannot see.
fitcheck           empty
fitcheck_neg       interferes
fitcheck_tilt      empty
fitcheck_tilt_neg  interferes
